# Copy to .env and fill in. All keys are optional — Jarvis degrades to keyless
# public endpoints for anything it has no key for, and says so when asked.

# Alchemy — EVM RPC, Portfolio API, Prices API. https://dashboard.alchemy.com
ALCHEMY_API_KEY=

# Helius — Solana RPC, DAS, Enhanced Transactions. https://dashboard.helius.dev
HELIUS_API_KEY=

# Optional
# DUNE_API_KEY=
# ARKHAM_API_KEY=

# ── Google Calendar & Meet (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Desktop-app OAuth client from https://console.cloud.google.com/
#   APIs & Services -> Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Desktop app
# Enable "Google Calendar API" (and "Google Meet API" for instant rooms).
# The "secret" is not secret for installed apps — Google's own flow puts it in
# the binary — which is why the exchange also uses PKCE. See googleCalendar.js.
#
# NOTE: creating a Google Meet LINK requires a paid Google Workspace account.
# On a personal Gmail the event is created without one, and Jarvis says so
# rather than pretending a link exists.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Filesystem reach (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Extra directories Jarvis may create files in, beyond Desktop, Documents,
# Downloads, Pictures, Videos and Music. Semicolon-separated, ABSOLUTE paths.
#
#   JARVIS_EXTRA_ROOTS=D:\Projects;C:\Work
#
# This is how you widen Jarvis's reach: you name the directories. The allowlist
# is not removed, because Jarvis acts on speech recognition and the guarantee
# worth keeping is not "Jarvis cannot write" but "a misheard word cannot write
# somewhere you did not choose". Set it to a drive root if you want that — the
# point is that it is your decision, written down.
JARVIS_EXTRA_ROOTS=

# ── Google Maps Platform (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Places API (New) supplies the globe's landmark labels. Without it the globe
# falls back to Wikipedia geosearch, which needs no key and no billing account.
# Enable "Places API (New)" at https://console.cloud.google.com/ and restrict
# the key to that API. Note two obligations that come with using it:
#   - Google's logo must be shown when their place data is drawn on a non-Google
#     map, which the Jarvis globe is.
#   - Place content may not be cached; only place_id is exempt.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# ── Luma events (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Puts the events from ONE Luma calendar onto the globe. Needs a Luma Plus
# subscription: lu.ma -> your calendar -> Settings -> Developer -> API Keys.
# NOTE: Luma has no public event search. The key is scoped to a single calendar,
# so this shows YOUR events wherever they are — it cannot discover other
# people's events in a city.
LUMA_API_KEY=
